Overview
========

"she_test_vectors" directory contains test vector(TV) files for SHE.

- SHE Test Vector files have .shx extension.
- Any file other than .shx extension will not be executed by SHE.
- TV will be executed in alphabetical order.


Current directory structure of she_test_vectors is:
--------------------------------------------------
she_test_vectors:
	- common : contain test vectors for API common for both seco and v2x
	- README
	- v2x : contain test vectors for API specific to v2x.
	  Currently it contains test vectors for FAST MAC MUBUFF V2 API
	  which are not applicable for i.MX8DXL DL3 board.
	- seco : (will be added later for seco specific API test vectors)

common:
	- add_keys
	- cipher
	- create_keystore
	- mac_generate
	- mac_verify
	- mac_verify_bit_ext
	- plain_key
	- rng
	- rng_uninited
	- status

v2x:
	- mac_generate
	- mac_verify
	- mac_verify_bit_ext

We have created separate files in most of the directories for
	- opening all required session and services and
	- closing the session and services

With this modular approach we dont need to complex our TV files with session
open and close commands and can keep the TV files specific to the test case.

We can keep session commands in same TV file also.

Test Vector Execution:
---------------------
V2X:
Two options are provided for executing the TVs:
	- by giving TV file name e.g.
		v2x_she_test file1.shx file2.shx

	- Execute all TVs in one go e.g.
		v2x_she_test -a

SECO:
Two options are provided for executing the TVs:
	- by giving TV file name e.g.
		seco_she_test file1.shx file2.shx

	- Execute all TVs in one go e.g.
		seco_she_test -a


Replace MU TYPE in Test Vector files:
----------------------------------

We have following supported SHE MU TYPE:
___________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________
|MU TYPE | Description												           |
|________|_________________________________________________________________________________________________________________|
|  0x48  | SHE MU on V2X												   |
|  0x08  | SHE MU on SECO												   |
|  0x49  | SHE1 MU on V2X (applicable for i.MX943 and i.MX95 board.)                                                       |
|        |    (To enable on i.MX95, please follow below steps:)                                                            |
|	 |    (NXP internal Users only)                                                                                    |
|        |	Please follow below page to enable SHE1 in linux for i.MX95 board:                                         |
|        |	https://confluence.sw.nxp.com/display/EPSTEC/i.MX95%3A+Steps+To+Enable+SHE1+AKA+SV1+and+SHE+NVM+on+DEBUG+MU|
|________|_________________________________________________________________________________________________________________|

By default, test vectors for SHE (test/she/she_test_vectors/), runs for MU_TYPE = 0x48.
If you want to run for other MU type, Ensure:
	- to change MU_TYPE in all the test-vector to correct value
		e.g. replace MU_TYPE 0x48 with MU_TYPE 0x08
			find ./ -type f | xargs sed -i 's/48 # MU_TYPE/08 # MU_TYPE/g'
	- board type should support intended MU_TYPE.

User application can refer:
get_supported_mu() in test/she/she_test_common.c file for reference implementation about MU_TYPE.

